# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile bosonic circuits {#transpile-bosonic-circuits}"
msgstr "Transpiler des circuits bosoniques {#transpile-bosonic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains how to transpile a [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") to a standard [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). A bosonic circuit carries no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit count (see [Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), so the transpiler is where those choices are made. The truncation and the encoding are described by a [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") (see [Describe the truncation with a LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)), and the mapper that turns operators into qubit operators is described in [Map operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation). The result is an ordinary [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit), so any Qiskit-compatible simulator can run it.\n"
msgstr "Ce guide explique comment transpiler un [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") en un [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) standard. Un circuit bosonique ne comporte ni troncature, ni encodage, ni nombre de qubits (voir [Travailler avec des circuits bosoniques](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), donc le transpileur est l'endroit où ces choix sont faits. La troncature et l'encodage sont décrits par une [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") (voir [Décrire la troncature avec une LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)), et le mapper qui transforme les opérateurs en opérateurs de qubits est décrit dans [Faire correspondre les représentations d'opérateurs](mappers#mappers-explanation). Le résultat est un [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) ordinaire, donc tout simulateur compatible avec Qiskit peut l'exécuter.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The guide uses one small example throughout: two bosonic modes, a state with one boson in each, and a single time evolution under a Bose-Hubbard Hamiltonian whose bond and on-site terms are in separate groups (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)):\n"
msgstr "Le guide utilise un petit exemple tout du long : deux modes bosoniques, un état avec un boson dans chacun, et une seule évolution temporelle sous un hamiltonien de Bose-Hubbard dont les termes de liaison et les termes sur site sont dans des groupes séparés (voir [Regrouper les termes d'un opérateur : utiliser la structure de l'opérateur](grouping#grouping-explanation)) :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation stages {#transpilation-stages}"
msgstr "Étapes de transpilation {#transpilation-stages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As explained in [`qiskit_bosons.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler#module-qiskit_bosons.transpiler \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler\"), the preset pass managers in this package split the transpilation into the following stages:\n"
msgstr "Comme expliqué dans [`qiskit_bosons.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler#module-qiskit_bosons.transpiler \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler\"), les gestionnaires de passes prédéfinis de ce paquet découpent la transpilation en les étapes suivantes :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Input** {#input}"
msgstr "**Entrée** {#input}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts the circuit to a directed acyclic graph (DAG) data structure, the representation that every later pass works on.\n"
msgstr "Convertit le circuit en une structure de données de graphe orienté acyclique (DAG), la représentation sur laquelle toutes les passes suivantes travaillent.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Optimization** {#optimization}"
msgstr "**Optimisation** {#optimization}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keeps the circuit in bosonic space. These passes use the structure of the bosonic operators, in particular their groups, while no qubit information exists yet. [`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") is the pass that breaks gates down here, with a plugin for each type of gate: a product formula or qDRIFT for an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\"), and the Clements mesh for a [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") (see [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) for how a method is chosen). [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") reorders the modes. The preset decomposes mode rotations in this stage and leaves everything else as it is.\n"
msgstr "Garde le circuit dans l'espace bosonique. Ces passes utilisent la structure des opérateurs bosoniques, en particulier leurs groupes, alors qu'aucune information de qubit n'existe encore. [`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") est la passe qui décompose ici les portes, avec un plugin pour chaque type de porte : une formule de produit ou qDRIFT pour une [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\"), et le maillage de Clements pour une [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") (voir [Synthétiser une porte Evolution dans l'espace bosonique](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) pour savoir comment une méthode est choisie). [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") réordonne les modes. Le préréglage décompose les rotations de modes à cette étape et laisse tout le reste tel quel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Layout** {#layout}"
msgstr "**Disposition** {#layout}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Maps each bosonic mode register to a quantum register. A bosonic mode generally occupies several qubits ($d$ of them under the unary encodings, $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ under the compact ones), so the quantum register is wider than the mode register. [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") derives the register width from a [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\").\n"
msgstr "Fait correspondre chaque registre de modes bosoniques à un registre quantique. Un mode bosonique occupe généralement plusieurs qubits ($d$ d'entre eux sous les encodages unaires, $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ sous les encodages compacts), donc le registre quantique est plus large que le registre de modes. [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") déduit la largeur du registre d'une [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Synthesis** {#synthesis}"
msgstr "**Synthèse** {#synthesis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts bosonic gates to qubit operations, one plugin per gate type. Encoding happens in this step: the plugin for an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate maps its operator to a qubit operator, and the plugin for an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate sets the qubits that encode each occupation. A barrier is carried onto every qubit of each register it touched.\n"
msgstr "Convertit les portes bosoniques en opérations sur qubits, un plugin par type de porte. L'encodage se produit à cette étape : le plugin d'une porte [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") fait correspondre son opérateur à un opérateur de qubits, et le plugin d'une porte [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") fixe les qubits qui encodent chaque occupation. Une barrière est reportée sur chaque qubit de chaque registre qu'elle touchait.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Qubit** {#qubit}"
msgstr "**Qubit** {#qubit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpiles the resulting qubit circuit with Qiskit’s own methods, for example to a basis gate set or a device. The preset always includes it; by default it is Qiskit’s preset pass manager, which synthesizes every evolution into gates (see [Continue on the qubit level](#transpilation-qubit-stage)).\n"
msgstr "Transpile le circuit de qubits obtenu avec les méthodes propres à Qiskit, par exemple vers un jeu de portes de base ou un dispositif. Le préréglage l'inclut toujours ; par défaut, c'est le gestionnaire de passes prédéfini de Qiskit, qui synthétise chaque évolution en portes (voir [Continuer au niveau des qubits](#transpilation-qubit-stage)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Output** {#output}"
msgstr "**Sortie** {#output}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts the internal DAG data structure back to a [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit).\n"
msgstr "Reconvertit la structure de données DAG interne en un [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The truncation and the encoding are not stored in the circuit. They are given to the transpiler, and the layout, the state preparation, and the mapper must all agree on them. The preset ensures that by handing the same [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") to all three.\n"
msgstr "La troncature et l'encodage ne sont pas stockés dans le circuit. Ils sont donnés au transpileur, et la disposition, la préparation d'état et le mapper doivent tous s'accorder sur eux. Le préréglage l'assure en transmettant la même [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") aux trois.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "A practical example {#a-practical-example}"
msgstr "Un exemple pratique {#a-practical-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-occupation-pass-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager\") builds the pipeline from a spec. Lowering the example under two encodings only changes the spec. The preset ends in Qiskit’s own qubit-level transpilation, which would synthesize the evolution into gates. To see the circuit exactly as the bosonic stages emit it, empty that stage first:\n"
msgstr "[`generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-occupation-pass-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager\") construit le pipeline à partir d'une spécification. Abaisser l'exemple sous deux encodages ne change que la spécification. Le préréglage se termine par la transpilation propre à Qiskit au niveau des qubits, qui synthétiserait l'évolution en portes. Pour voir le circuit exactement tel que les étapes bosoniques l'émettent, vide d'abord cette étape :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two encodings use six and four qubits respectively (three levels per mode under the unary encoding, two qubits per mode under the Gray code), but the structure of the circuit is the same: two [`XGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XGate) operations prepare the occupations, and one [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) carries the evolution.\n"
msgstr "Les deux encodages utilisent respectivement six et quatre qubits (trois niveaux par mode sous l'encodage unaire, deux qubits par mode sous le code de Gray), mais la structure du circuit est la même : deux opérations [`XGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XGate) préparent les occupations, et un [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) porte l'évolution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare with the traditional workflow {#compare-with-the-traditional-workflow}"
msgstr "Comparaison avec le flux de travail traditionnel {#compare-with-the-traditional-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation) guide describes the traditional workflow, which maps the Hamiltonian to a qubit operator *before* it builds the [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). The two routes produce equivalent circuits. They differ in what has to be redone when the truncation changes. The bosonic circuit is built once and lowered at every cutoff, whereas the map-first route needs the operator mapped again and the circuit rebuilt:\n"
msgstr "Le guide sur les [circuits bosoniques](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation) décrit le flux de travail traditionnel, qui fait correspondre le hamiltonien à un opérateur de qubits *avant* de construire le [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). Les deux voies produisent des circuits équivalents. Elles diffèrent par ce qu'il faut refaire lorsque la troncature change. Le circuit bosonique est construit une fois et abaissé à chaque coupure, alors que la voie qui applique d'abord la correspondance exige de refaire la correspondance de l'opérateur et de reconstruire le circuit :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entangling-gate count depends on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution gate, which changes between releases, so plot it:\n"
msgstr "Le nombre de portes intriquantes dépend de la façon dont Qiskit synthétise la porte d'évolution, ce qui change d'une version à l'autre, donc trace-le :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![CX count of the lowered circuit against the number of levels d, growing quickly with d.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/transpilation-4.avif)\n"
msgstr "![CX count of the lowered circuit against the number of levels d, growing quickly with d.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/transpilation-4.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The count grows quickly with the cutoff, which is the reason to keep the cutoff a parameter of the transpilation and not of the circuit. The two routes are equivalent here, but only the bosonic one can also interleave the grouping of the operator with the product formula (see [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation)) or hand the encoding to a different spec without changing a line of the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Le nombre croît rapidement avec la coupure, ce qui justifie de garder la coupure comme paramètre de la transpilation et non du circuit. Les deux voies sont équivalentes ici, mais seule la voie bosonique peut aussi entrelacer le regroupement de l'opérateur avec la formule de produit (voir [Synthétiser une porte Evolution dans l'espace bosonique](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation)) ou confier l'encodage à une autre spécification sans changer une ligne du circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A spec with a single cutoff leaves the number of modes open, so one pass manager serves circuits of any width. A spec with one cutoff per mode fixes the width:\n"
msgstr "Une spécification avec une seule coupure laisse le nombre de modes ouvert, donc un seul gestionnaire de passes sert des circuits de n'importe quelle largeur. Une spécification avec une coupure par mode fixe la largeur :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the pipeline by hand {#build-the-pipeline-by-hand}"
msgstr "Construire le pipeline à la main {#build-the-pipeline-by-hand}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The preset is a [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager) with one entry per stage. You can assemble the same pipeline from its parts, which is the starting point for every customization below:\n"
msgstr "Le preset est un [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager) avec une entrée par étape. Tu peux assembler le même pipeline à partir de ses éléments, ce qui est le point de départ de toutes les personnalisations ci-dessous :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The mapper function receives an operator and the width of the register that the layout derived, and returns a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable). Because it is given the width, passing `num_qubits` on to [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") makes the mapper check that the spec fits the register, so a mismatch between the layout and the encoding fails with a clear message.\n"
msgstr "La fonction de mapper reçoit un opérateur et la largeur du registre que le layout a déduite, et renvoie un [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable). Comme la largeur lui est fournie, transmettre `num_qubits` à [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") fait vérifier au mapper que la spécification tient dans le registre, de sorte qu'une incohérence entre le layout et l'encodage échoue avec un message clair.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Advanced workflows {#advanced-workflows}"
msgstr "Workflows avancés {#advanced-workflows}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Provide an explicit layout {#provide-an-explicit-layout}"
msgstr "Fournir un layout explicite {#provide-an-explicit-layout}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`CustomB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-custom-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.CustomB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.CustomB2QLayout\") replaces the layout stage with a mapping that you provide, from each bosonic register of the circuit to a quantum register. It is useful when the register must be wider than the spec needs, for example to leave idle qubits for other purposes:\n"
msgstr "[`CustomB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-custom-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.CustomB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.CustomB2QLayout\") remplace l'étape de layout par une correspondance que tu fournis, de chaque registre bosonique du circuit vers un registre quantique. Elle est utile lorsque le registre doit être plus large que ce dont la spécification a besoin, par exemple pour laisser des qubits inactifs à d'autres fins :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  A custom layout is your responsibility. The synthesis plugins still address qubits through the spec, so a register that does not match the spec’s widths gives a wrong circuit or an error deep inside a plugin. A custom layout also skips the check that [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") performs after [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") (see the next section).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Avertissement\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Un layout personnalisé est de ta responsabilité. Les plugins de synthèse adressent toujours les qubits via la spécification ; un registre qui ne correspond pas aux largeurs de la spécification produit donc un circuit erroné ou une erreur au fond d'un plugin. Un layout personnalisé ignore aussi la vérification que [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") effectue après [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") (voir la section suivante).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reorder the modes {#reorder-the-modes}"
msgstr "Réordonner les modes {#reorder-the-modes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") is an optimization-stage pass that reorders the modes. The permutation is read as a mapping from original to new mode index, and it is recorded in the circuit metadata. The reordering changes which qubits each mode occupies, and so it can reduce the depth of the lowered circuit.\n"
msgstr "[`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") est une passe de l'étape d'optimisation qui réordonne les modes. La permutation est lue comme une correspondance de l'indice de mode d'origine vers le nouvel indice, et elle est enregistrée dans les métadonnées du circuit. Le réordonnancement change les qubits qu'occupe chaque mode, et peut donc réduire la profondeur du circuit abaissé.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the result is expressed in the new mode order, measured bitstrings must be mapped back before they are interpreted. With several qubits per mode, the mapping acts on blocks of qubits and not on single bits. The following example relabels three modes, each occupying two qubits under the Gray code, and recovers the original occupation from the measured counts:\n"
msgstr "Comme le résultat est exprimé dans le nouvel ordre des modes, les chaînes de bits mesurées doivent être remises dans l'ordre d'origine avant d'être interprétées. Avec plusieurs qubits par mode, la correspondance agit sur des blocs de qubits et non sur des bits isolés. L'exemple suivant renomme trois modes, chacun occupant deux qubits sous le code de Gray, et retrouve l'occupation d'origine à partir des comptages mesurés :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The restored bitstring is what the circuit produces without the relabeling, read in Qiskit’s little-endian order: mode 0 holds the Gray code of level two (`11`), mode 1 holds level zero (`00`), and mode 2 holds level one (`01`).\n"
msgstr "La chaîne de bits restaurée est ce que le circuit produit sans le renommage, lue dans l'ordre little-endian de Qiskit : le mode 0 contient le code de Gray du niveau deux (`11`), le mode 1 le niveau zéro (`00`) et le mode 2 le niveau un (`01`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Warning\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Avertissement\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  A spec that gives the modes **different** cutoffs cannot be combined with [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\"). The cutoffs are attached to the modes by their position, so reordering the modes would put a cutoff on the wrong mode. [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") refuses a relabeled circuit in that case:\n"
msgstr "  Une spécification qui donne aux modes des cutoffs **différents** ne peut pas être combinée avec [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\"). Les cutoffs sont rattachés aux modes par leur position ; réordonner les modes placerait donc un cutoff sur le mauvais mode. [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") refuse un circuit renommé dans ce cas :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the synthesis plugins {#choose-the-synthesis-plugins}"
msgstr "Choisir les plugins de synthèse {#choose-the-synthesis-plugins}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\") has no default plugins; the preset registers one per gate type. The available plugins are managed by [`B2QSynthesisPluginManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-b-2-q-synthesis-plugin-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.B2QSynthesisPluginManager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.B2QSynthesisPluginManager\"), which lists them by the name of the gate they act on:\n"
msgstr "[`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\") n'a aucun plugin par défaut ; le preset en enregistre un par type de porte. Les plugins disponibles sont gérés par [`B2QSynthesisPluginManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-b-2-q-synthesis-plugin-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.B2QSynthesisPluginManager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.B2QSynthesisPluginManager\"), qui les liste par le nom de la porte sur laquelle ils agissent :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two builtin methods are `Evolution.MapperFn` and `InitializeModes.Occupation`. The first synthesizes an evolution from any mapper function, which is how a custom encoding is plugged in (see [Map operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation)). The library ships no plugin for a [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") gate. The preset breaks it down in bosonic space into [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gates first, which the first method then handles, but a plugin registered for `ModeRotation` can lower the gate directly instead; see [Rotate bosonic modes](mode-rotation#mode-rotation-explanation) and [Lower a rotation without decomposing it](mode-rotation#mode-rotation-direct-explanation). You can register a method by name through the `config` argument of [`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\"), or write a plugin object into [`B2QSynthesis.methods`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis.methods \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis.methods\") directly, as the preceding examples do.\n"
msgstr "Les deux méthodes intégrées sont `Evolution.MapperFn` et `InitializeModes.Occupation`. La première synthétise une évolution à partir de n'importe quelle fonction de mapper, ce qui permet de brancher un encodage personnalisé (voir [Map operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation)). La bibliothèque ne fournit aucun plugin pour une porte [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\"). Le preset la décompose d'abord dans l'espace bosonique en portes [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\"), que la première méthode traite ensuite, mais un plugin enregistré pour `ModeRotation` peut abaisser la porte directement ; voir [Rotate bosonic modes](mode-rotation#mode-rotation-explanation) et [Lower a rotation without decomposing it](mode-rotation#mode-rotation-direct-explanation). Tu peux enregistrer une méthode par son nom via l'argument `config` de [`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\"), ou écrire directement un objet plugin dans [`B2QSynthesis.methods`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis.methods \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis.methods\"), comme le font les exemples précédents.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpilation-qubit-stage\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Continue on the qubit level {#continue-on-the-qubit-level}"
msgstr "Poursuivre au niveau des qubits {#continue-on-the-qubit-level}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The preset always ends in a `qubit` stage, which is Qiskit’s own preset pass manager. Keyword arguments of [`generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-occupation-pass-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager\") are handed to [`qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager), so you can translate to a basis gate set or target a device directly. Prefer `optimization_level=0` to keep the circuit close to what the bosonic stages produced:\n"
msgstr "Le preset se termine toujours par une étape `qubit`, qui est le pass manager prédéfini propre à Qiskit. Les arguments nommés de [`generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-occupation-pass-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager\") sont transmis à [`qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager), ce qui te permet de traduire vers un ensemble de portes de base ou de cibler directement un dispositif. Préfère `optimization_level=0` pour garder le circuit proche de ce que les étapes bosoniques ont produit :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two other choices are common. Assign an empty [`PassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.PassManager) to the `qubit` stage when you want to show the circuit exactly as the pipeline synthesized it, as the examples above do. Or assemble the pipeline yourself and add any Qiskit pass manager as the `qubit` stage of the [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager). Stages run in the order they are given, so the `qubit` stage must come before `output`, because Qiskit’s passes expect a DAG and not a finished circuit:\n"
msgstr "Deux autres choix sont courants. Affecte un [`PassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.PassManager) vide à l'étape `qubit` lorsque tu veux montrer le circuit exactement tel que le pipeline l'a synthétisé, comme le font les exemples ci-dessus. Ou assemble toi-même le pipeline et ajoute n'importe quel pass manager de Qiskit comme étape `qubit` du [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager). Les étapes s'exécutent dans l'ordre où elles sont données ; l'étape `qubit` doit donc venir avant `output`, car les passes de Qiskit attendent un DAG et non un circuit terminé :\n"

